- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests`

**How to implement.** The start-up imports whose rows wait open the import dialog from the Launcher (001 §B; .spec-md §3.7: rows that need a choice wait in the one import dialog, their default pre-selected, and nothing in them applies unconfirmed; §10.1: the dialog opens at start when a catalogue row needs a choice; S3.1 step 100 holds them in `AppContext.pendingImports`). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow` (steps 88, 89): (1) For `Ok context`, the window keeps the imports still waiting in one local mutable list, started from `context.pendingImports`; the window is the IO edge (AGENTS.md: mutation only at the IO boundary). While the list is not empty, the content shows, between the title and the surface buttons, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.launcherPendingImportsText` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, with the text `Library entries waiting for an import decision: <n>.` (`n` summing the `decisions` of the list), and a `Button` carrying `launcherReviewImportsButton` the same way, labelled `Review imports…`. Its click opens `ImportDialogWindow(context.catalogueImports, SettlePendingCatalogue head, onApplied)` (step 108) over the head of the list. `onApplied` removes from the list the import whose `entry.catalogueId` is the applied request's, and rebuilds the content through step 89's local content function, so the notice counts what still waits and goes when nothing does. Cancel leaves the list as it was. (2) The first time the launcher opens (`Opened`), when the list is not empty, it opens the dialog over its head, so the choice is asked at start; the launcher never applies a row itself. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group: `launcherPendingImportsText` (`"LauncherPendingImportsText"`) and `launcherReviewImportsButton` (`"LauncherReviewImportsButton"`), each with a one-line doc. (4) Tests, in `LauncherTests`. `a launcher with no pending import shows no import notice`: in `withLauncher` (the fixture explicitly settles the Built-in catalogue before opening the launcher) neither id is present, and the buttons are still the four surfaces. `acceptance: a start-up catalogue whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog from the launcher; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply settles it` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `TestAppScope.fileLocations`, a first `AppContext.create` saves a user material `Lab glass` through its `materials`; the `Builtin` folder under the locations' `shippedCatalogueFolder` is rewritten with a new-id material named `Lab glass` (step 100's `create holds every changed-catalogue row pending and writes nothing before confirmation` setup); and a second `AppContext.create` holds one pending import containing every catalogue decision row. `LauncherWindow(locations, WorkbenchSettings.defaults, Ok ctx)` shown headless opens exactly one `ImportDialogWindow`, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent`, and `launcherPendingImportsText` reads `Library entries waiting for an import decision: <all pending rows>.`. Pressing the dialog's `importCancelButton` closes it and keeps the notice. Clicking `launcherReviewImportsButton` opens a dialog again. Pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, removes the notice and the button, and leaves both `Lab glass` materials held. A third `AppContext.create` over the same locations holds no pending import. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher, whose context holds no pending import, keeps its code. The headless startup acceptance fact MUST also run on a fresh empty database with a nonconflicting catalogue: the dialog MUST show every Add and Reuse row, Cancel MUST leave entries and the log unchanged, and Apply MUST settle the whole list. Mixed-conflict coverage MUST remain. The test MUST derive its displayed row count from the complete decisions list, not a collision count; fixture population elsewhere MUST explicitly settle first.

**Acceptance.** After the launcher is wired, a start-up import whose rows await MUST open `ImportDialogWindow` from the launcher and stay waiting until Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a start-up catalogue whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog from the launcher; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply settles it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a launcher with no pending import shows no import notice`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
